      "writtenOn": "2023-07-19T21:09:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this check will only succeed on the CBI layout we\u0027ve chosen for\nthe 1MB part. it\u0027s going to fail on the layout for 512KB parts.\n`CONFIG_FLASH_ERASE_SIZE` isn\u0027t really a good check.\n\nalso, given the assumptions made in the erase loop below,\nwe need to check some additional limitations.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 480,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 480,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "5dba56923bde36d7adf9bf7527a9ea78cf6191c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09c1950f_eef65fe0",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_npcx.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 480,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T04:03:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The upstream driver has the check. I think we can remove it too.\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/zephyr/+/refs/heads/main/drivers/flash/spi_nor.c#748\n\nThe difference is the upstream driver does the 4K (section erase) check but execute either the 4K erase or the 64K erase (block erase) commands depending on the size. On the other hand, the legacy EC implementation check and erase the same size defined in `CONFIG_FLASH_ERASE_SIZE`.\n\nIn this shim layer, the alignment checks seem meaningless. It tries to carry over the legacy EC concept to Zephyr.\n\nThe purpose of the below loop is for reloading the watchdog timer, i.e.  crrev.com/c/4118799. Erasing the entire flash like 512KB triggers the watchdog. Breaking it down to the `CONFIG_FLASH_ERASE_SIZE` fixes it. One iteration can be 64KB or even larger like 128KB.",
